WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.900
[The] insect control people in plant pathology was having a problem with controlling ratoon stunting disease.

2
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:20.060
And the method that they were using was referred to as heated air applied to the sugarcane to kill the disease.

3
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.720
Well, they approached us.

4
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.480
It could have been the extension people.

5
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:30.620
No, it was the plant pathology people that approached us for some help in developing a system.

6
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:43.260
So to make a long story short we developed what we called an aerated steam system where we applied steam to the heated air and they would kill the disease.

7
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:56.000
It being steam, the water transferred the heat more efficiently and effectively through the treatment box or whatever it was doing.

8
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:05.680
And compared to hot water, well the water was such that it actually killed the buds on the seedlings.

9
00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.360
So we were kind of in between with the aerated steam.

10
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:24.620
So that was one instance to where . . . then some of the farmer . . . the extension people introduced this to co-ops and the farmers and even manufacturers and it was used within the industry.
